From 625eb9a3d5aadb74579ca174c86c6aad11207220 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miures Manager <contact@miures.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:06:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Research Engine Phase 5: chart choice by purpose and
 audience, the storytelling deck, Word documents, output by sentence, the
 narrative gate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Research Engine audit's Phase 5 (automated reporting), on top of
Phases 1–4. "Create the client-ready research proposal" and "create the
final findings presentation" produce the right file. Nothing existing was
removed: the report blocks, templates, PowerPoint and Excel exports and
the Reports panel are as they were; the new documents reuse their drawing.

Analytics: chartPurpose.ts (the purpose read from the analysis — comparison,
composition, distribution, trend, relationship, ranking, KPI, significance,
profile — and the audience adjust the shape-based chart scores, never past
what the data can draw); deck.ts (the story in a fixed order: summary, key
findings with the chart for the audience and the so-what, who differs,
statistical highlights, beyond the plan, implications, recommendations,
method, caveats — every sentence from the run); export/deck.ts (one builder
per slide type on a type ramp, palette and grid; flat native charts; the
dimensional treatment on covers, dividers and callouts); export/docx.ts
(the research proposal from the design; the findings report from a run);
narrative.ts (the model's headline, summary, implications and
recommendations gated sentence by sentence against the run's numbers,
hypotheses and verdicts). Two wordings fixed: a one-test "not supported"
verdict read "is significant"; a test planned by sentence listed its
outcome twice.

Engine: the `output` interpretation kind — the proposal, the findings
report or the deck from the sentence's noun, the audience from its words
("for the board", "for the analysts"), the client from "for Acme"; an
executive summary in words, a report to draft in the workspace or an edit
in the same sentence stay the model's.

Studio: POST /api/copilot/output (project.read for the proposal,
analytics.export for the findings outputs; the sandbox against the fake
provider sends its own definition, rows and a scripted narrative); the
narrative call metered as copilot_narrative; the card holds the file with
its size, what it holds and what the gate kept; the Findings tab's
Documents buttons are sentences the engine reads.

Tests: analytics 253 (phase5.test 6), engine 1749 (the Phase 5 block of
nlPhase4.test), studio 284, scripts/phase5-reporting-test.mjs (6 checks);
full browser corpus green apart from the 10 known baseline failures.
Mutations: analytics 30/30, engine 6/6, Studio 10/10 caught. See
docs/PHASE5-REPORTING-2026-10-09.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
