@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Research Engine — Phase 5: Automated reporting (09-10-2026)
+
+**Source:** the Research Engine audit (`RESEARCH-ENGINE-AUDIT-2026-10-08.md`, section K, Phase 5), on top of Phases 1–4. The outcome it set: *"create the client-ready research proposal" and "create the final findings presentation" produce the right file.* Every change has a regression test and the tests were mutation-checked. Nothing existing was removed: the report blocks, the templates, the PowerPoint and Excel exports and the Reports panel are as they were; the new documents sit beside them and reuse their drawing code.
+
+## Checklist
+
+| ID | Audit finding (§B.4, §C.4, §I) | Change | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| R1 | Chart selection reads the result's shape only — not the analytical purpose, not the audience | `chartPurpose.ts`: the purpose read from the analysis (comparison, composition, distribution, trend, relationship, ranking, KPI, significance, profile) and an audience (executive, client, researcher) adjust the shape-based scores — the types that serve the purpose are lifted, whole families lifted or lowered for the audience — never past what the data can draw; the reason names both | ✅ Added |
+| R2 | PowerPoint has fixed basic layouts, no design system, no storytelling structure, no statistical-highlight or implications/recommendations slides | `deck.ts` + `export/deck.ts`: the story in a fixed order — title, summary, key findings (one per slide, the chart chosen for the audience, the one sentence that says why it matters, a significance badge), who differs (segment comparison with the groups), statistical highlights (the statistic as a callout card), beyond the plan, implications, recommendations, method, caveats — on one type ramp, palette and grid; flat native charts, the dimensional treatment on covers, dividers and callouts only, as the audit recommends | ✅ Added |
+| R3 | No research-design / proposal Word document | `buildProposalDocx`: cover, background and objective, research questions and KPIs, hypotheses with their readings and the questions that measure them, constructs, the questionnaire by section with a length estimate, sample and the base the plan needs, the analysis plan with its reasons, deliverables, assumptions and sources — from the design alone | ✅ Added |
+| R4 | No findings Word document | `buildFindingsDocx`: executive summary, the verdicts (with the corrected reading), each key finding with its so-what, evidence and groups, who differs, beyond the plan, the data advice, what it means, what to do next, the method, every finding with its test and adjusted p, caveats; chart data as tables | ✅ Added |
+| R5 | No output-type intelligence: "create the client-ready research proposal" went to the model, which had nothing to produce | the engine reads *create the client-ready research proposal*, *write the research design document for Acme*, *create the final findings presentation*, *create the findings deck for the board*, *build the results deck for the analysts*, *write the findings report as a Word document*, *make a Word document of the findings* into an `output` interpretation — the type from the noun, the audience from the words, the client from "for …"; the Studio's output route makes the file; the Findings tab offers each as a button that is a sentence | ✅ Added |
+| R6 | Narrative sections only via a model turn, unchecked | `narrative.ts`: the model is asked once, from the run's brief and nothing else, for a headline, summary, implications and recommendations; the gate checks every sentence — each number must be one the run printed, each hypothesis must exist and keep its verdict — and drops what fails, with the reason; what it kept replaces the engine's words, never the numbers; the card says what was kept and dropped | ✅ Added |
+| R7 | A one-test "not supported" verdict read "The planned test is significant" | the verdict says "The planned test is not significant" | ✅ Fixed |
+| R8 | A test planned by sentence (Phase 4) listed its outcome twice, so its finding read "SAT across GENDER and SAT" | `planBridge` lists each variable once | ✅ Fixed |
+
+## What was built
+
+**Chart choice (`packages/analytics/src/chartPurpose.ts`)** — `purposeOf(def, result)` reads why a result is shown: a crosstab compares, a test shows a difference with its uncertainty, a correlation or model relates, a descriptive spreads, NPS is a number to watch, ranking and MaxDiff rank, segmentation profiles, time-like categories are a trend whatever the kind. `chooseChart(def, result, { purpose?, audience? })` starts from `recommendCharts` (the shape), lifts the types that serve the purpose (bars for a comparison, stacked-100 and donuts for a composition, the histogram for a distribution, the line for a trend, the scatter for a relationship, ranked bars for a ranking, the KPI card, the interval chart or the bars for significance) and lifts or lowers families for the audience (an executive loses the statistical and significance families and gains bars and KPIs; a researcher gains the significance family). A chart the data cannot draw is never a candidate; the reason names the purpose and the audience with their weights.
+
+**The deck (`deck.ts`, `export/deck.ts`)** — `deckFromRun(def, run, { audience, client, maxFindings, narrative, results })` tells the story: the title; the summary (objective, verdicts, the strongest findings, what was found beyond the plan); a key finding per significant planned finding, strongest first, with the chart chosen for the audience, the evidence line (test, p, effect, n, the adjusted p) and the so-what (the hypothesis it is evidence for and its verdict; a strong or moderate effect "worth acting on", a small one "real, but modest"; a corrected-away finding "read with caution"); who differs (the groups highest first, the pairs that differ); statistical highlights (the effect as a callout); beyond the plan (the discoveries not already shown, the anomalies as caveats); implications (each verdict against the design); recommendations (lead with the strongest finding, treat a corrected-away one with caution, re-run an inconclusive one, plan the test an untested one lacks, add a discovery to the plan, re-run as the data advises); method; caveats. `buildDeckPptx` draws it with one builder per slide type on `DECK_STYLE` (display 36 / title 22 / headline 17 / body 12 / caption 9 / statistic 40), the theme's palette and fonts, a kicker per slide, the significance badge, cards with a soft shadow, native editable charts through the existing `drawAnalysisVisual`.
+
+**The documents (`export/docx.ts`)** — both on the `docx` library the questionnaire export uses, with the same page and type conventions. The proposal needs no data: it is written from the survey and its research design, with the engine's readings (`structuredHypotheses`, `explainPlan`, `planSampleSize`, `expectedSample`, `inferRole`). The findings report is written from a run through the same `deckFromRun` story, with the groups and the chart data as tables.
+
+**Output by sentence (`packages/engine/src/nlIntent.ts`, the `output` kind)** — the recogniser reads the verb, the modifiers (client-ready, final, full, executive, findings …), the noun (proposal / research design document; presentation / deck / slides / PowerPoint; findings report / report as a Word document / Word document of the findings) and the tail ("for the board" is an executive edition, "for the analysts" a researcher's, "for Acme Ltd" the client, "for this survey" nothing); a tail it cannot read, an edit in the same sentence, an executive summary in words or a report to draft in the analytics workspace stay the model's. A bare survey is refused with what to record first.
+
+**The Studio** — `POST /api/copilot/output` (`project.read` for the proposal, `analytics.export` for the findings outputs; the sandbox against the fake provider sends its own definition, rows and a scripted narrative): the proposal from the design with the project's client and fieldwork dates; the findings outputs from a fresh `runPlan` on the clean live data; the narrative from the model (metered, `copilot_narrative`) through `gateNarrative`; the file as the response with `content-disposition`, what it holds and what the gate kept in headers. `useCopilot.makeOutput` shows the file on the card (`cp-output`: name, size, a download link, the summary, the narrative gate's verdict); `IntelligentView` routes the `output` kind there; the Findings tab's *Documents* section offers the proposal, the findings report, the findings deck and the executive deck as sentences the engine reads.
+
+## Tests
+
+| Suite | What it checks | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| `packages/analytics/src/phase5.test.ts` | the purpose of each analysis kind and of time-like categories; the audience's effect (interval chart for a researcher, bars for an executive), an asked purpose, never an undrawable chart; the deck's order, title, summary, key findings with so-what and evidence, the relationship's scatter, the small effect's wording, groups highest first, the pairs, the highlights, implications and recommendations, method, the analysis ids, the executive deck, the narrative replacing words not numbers, the unshown discovery beyond the plan, no empty section, the single-test verdict wording, the caveat slide; the gate's numbers, hypotheses, verdicts, counting words, years, percentages, the section-by-section result; the PowerPoint (one slide per story slide, the design system's words, the badge, the callout, native charts, the missing-result note); the proposal's every section and a bare survey; the findings report's every section, a narrative, the advice table | 6 tests (analytics 253 pass) |
+| `packages/engine/src/nlPhase4.test.ts` (Phase 5 block) | every sentence form, the audience and client tails, what stays the model's, the bare-survey refusal | 1 test (engine 1749 pass) |
+| `scripts/phase5-reporting-test.mjs` (browser) | the proposal from the design on the card; findings outputs without respondents refused; the deck from injected rows with a scripted narrative — the gate keeping five of six sentences and naming the dropped one; the Word report with the engine's words when the model has nothing; the Findings tab's Documents buttons (executive edition, proposal); the output route's gate | 6 checks |
+
+Existing wording fixed on purpose: `findings.ts` (R7) and `planBridge.ts` (R8) — no existing test asserted the wrong text.
+
+Mutation checks: analytics 30 mutations, all caught after four tests were strengthened; engine 6 mutations, all caught (two re-run as compile-safe variants); Studio surfaces 10 mutations through the browser suite, all caught.
+
+The full browser corpus (133 suites) is green apart from the 10 known baseline failures; `distribution-test.mjs` failed once in the corpus on a cold server (its 10-second wait for the first compile of the respondents route) and passes on a warm one — not a regression.
